        "type": "text",
        "text": "{\"id\":\"e0607ce5-7d2f-48bd-ab0b-0242c445dfc7\",\"title\":\"Architecture & Delivery Plan — SFN-20: Build mdfn as the Superfunctions Markdown authoring platform\",\"content\":\"Backlog issue: [SFN-20 — Build mdfn as the Superfunctions Markdown authoring platform](<https://linear.app/21n/issue/SFN-20/build-mdfn-as-the-superfunctions-markdown-authoring-platform>)\\n\\n## Architecture objective\\n\\nDeliver a modular Markdown platform whose core semantics are independent of UI framework, storage, transport, collaboration provider, and product surface.\\n\\nThe architecture must support a progression from parser/serializer use to visual editing and optional collaborative services without replacing the durable Markdown contract.\\n\\n## Non-negotiable architecture rules\\n\\n 1. Markdown source is always present in the durable snapshot.\\n 2. Runtime structured state is versioned, derived, and invalidated by schema/source identity.\\n 3. Unsupported constructs survive as opaque, diagnosable content.\\n 4. Core commands and transactions cannot import DOM, UI, framework, server, or product packages.\\n 5. Framework adapters bind shared behavior and cannot fork it.\\n 6. UIFn owns editor chrome; mdfn owns editing semantics.\\n 7. Optional server packages use shared HTTP, database, authentication, and file abstractions.\\n 8. Database adapters are wrapped internally with the mdfn schema.\\n 9. Raw HTML is disabled by default and every rendering/import boundary has a security policy.\\n10. Extension behavior is defined once and validated by conformance suites.\\n\\n## Layered system\\n\\n```text\\nMarkdown source and sidecar metadata\\n                ↓\\n@mdfn/markdown: parse, serialize, format, diagnose, source map\\n                ↓\\n@mdfn/core: schema, document, transactions, commands, history, extensions\\n                ↓\\n@mdfn/dom + @mdfn/source: browser editing and source editing\\n                ↓\\n@mdfn/adapter-kit\\n       ↙             ↓             ↘\\n@mdfn/react     @mdfn/svelte    @mdfn/solid\\n       ↘             ↓             ↙\\n@mdfn/components + framework component bindings + UIFn\\n                ↓\\noptional collab, server, files, content, search, AI bridges\\n```\\n\\nRendering can consume the Markdown pipeline directly or project structured documents into safe HTML without loading browser editing packages.\\n\\n## Proposed package graph\\n\\n### Stable foundation\\n\\n* `@mdfn/core` — schema, nodes, marks, selections, steps, transactions, commands, history, extension registry, versioning, migrations\\n* `@mdfn/markdown` — CommonMark/GFM pipeline, positional AST, source spans, parsing, serialization, formatting, diagnostics, preservation metadata\\n* `@mdfn/render` — safe HTML and render-tree output, sanitization hooks, read-only render policies\\n* `@mdfn/dom` — DOM editor view, events, selection bridge, clipboard, drag/drop, composition, input handling, node views\\n* `@mdfn/source` — source editor state, syntax highlighting integration, source diagnostics, source/visual synchronization\\n* `@mdfn/extensions` — supported extension packs exposed through subpath exports\\n* `@mdfn/adapter-kit` — lifecycle, subscription, action, and renderer contracts shared by framework bindings\\n* `@mdfn/react`\\n* `@mdfn/svelte`\\n* `@mdfn/solid`\\n* `@mdfn/components` — framework-neutral component recipes and editor UI contracts\\n* `@mdfn/components-react`\\n* `@mdfn/components-svelte`\\n* `@mdfn/components-solid`\\n* `@mdfn/testing` — corpus, traces, fixtures, harnesses, extension certification\\n* `@mdfn/registry` — optional registry metadata and installation composition\\n* `mdfn` — curated facade for common use cases\\n\\n### Optional platform packages\\n\\n* `@mdfn/collab` — provider-neutral collaborative state, awareness, comments, suggestions, history contracts\\n* `@mdfn/client` — client for self-hosted document and collaboration services\\n* `@mdfn/server` — HTTP routes, persistence services, authorization hooks, migrations\\n* `@mdfn/filefn` — FileFn asset-provider bridge\\n* `@mdfn/contentfn` — explicit Markdown content-type bridge\\n* `@mdfn/searchfn` — indexing and extraction bridge\\n* `@mdfn/ai` — provider-neutral assistant actions expressed as reviewable transactions or suggestions\\n\\nExtension packs should use subpath exports rather than one workspace package per node or mark.\\n\\n## Dependency policy\\n\\nAllowed dependencies flow downward only:\\n\\n* Markdown may depend on core types that are environment-neutral.\\n* Render may depend on core and Markdown.\\n* DOM and source may depend on core, Markdown, and render.\\n* Adapter kit may …3329 tokens truncated…s cover representative input methods.\\n* Clipboard fixtures cover internal, Markdown, HTML, office-like, and plain-text sources.\\n* Source/visual switching preserves document and selection expectations.\\n* Keystroke, parse, and memory budgets pass representative large documents.\\n* SSR imports are side-effect safe.\\n\\n### Phase 3 — Framework adapters and UI\\n\\nDeliver:\\n\\n* Adapter kit\\n* React, Svelte, and Solid packages\\n* Headless and styled editor components\\n* UIFn-based toolbar, bubble controls, command palette, links, tables, files, outline, diagnostics\\n* Registry composition\\n* Framework examples and packed consumers\\n\\nExit criteria:\\n\\n* Every semantic trace passes for vanilla DOM, React, Svelte, and Solid.\\n* No framework package owns unique editor semantics.\\n* Accessibility checks cover keyboard navigation, screen readers, focus, dialogs, and high contrast.\\n* SSR/hydration examples pass for supported framework environments.\\n* Package graph verifier passes with zero forbidden edges.\\n\\n### Phase 4 — Ecosystem adoption\\n\\nDeliver:\\n\\n* DocsFn canonical parser integration and compatibility projection\\n* Explicit ContentFn Markdown type\\n* CmsFn authoring integration\\n* FileFn asset provider\\n* SearchFn extraction bridge\\n* Migration and compatibility tooling\\n\\nExit criteria:\\n\\n* Existing DocsFn fixtures pass or have approved documented migrations.\\n* ContentFn storage remains explicit and versioned.\\n* CmsFn can author, preview, save, reload, and migrate Markdown content.\\n* File references survive save/reload and authorization changes.\\n* Search output matches canonical document interpretation.\\n* Downstream packages consume public APIs only.\\n\\n### Phase 5 — Collaboration and editorial platform\\n\\nDeliver:\\n\\n* Collaboration provider contracts and implementation\\n* Client/server packages\\n* Presence and offline synchronization\\n* Comments, suggestions, review state, and history\\n* AuthFn/HTTP/database integrations\\n* Operational diagnostics and compaction\\n\\nExit criteria:\\n\\n* Concurrent and offline edit simulations converge.\\n* Anchors survive representative edits and migrations.\\n* Incompatible schemas are negotiated or rejected safely.\\n* Authorization and audit tests cover document, comment, suggestion, asset, and history operations.\\n* Persistence recovery and compaction tests pass.\\n* Multi-user performance budgets pass.\\n\\n## Verification matrix\\n\\n### Parser and serializer\\n\\n* CommonMark corpus\\n* GFM corpus\\n* Extension fixtures\\n* No-edit byte identity\\n* Semantic round trips\\n* Touched-region normalization\\n* Unknown and disabled syntax\\n* Line endings and Unicode\\n* Malformed and adversarial input\\n* Migration chains\\n\\n### Core engine\\n\\n* Transaction invertibility\\n* Position mapping\\n* Selection mapping\\n* History grouping\\n* Command availability\\n* Plugin isolation\\n* Schema validation\\n* Diagnostics\\n* Deterministic snapshots\\n* Sidecar anchor mapping\\n\\n### Browser\\n\\n* Chrome, Firefox, Safari\\n* Desktop and mobile viewports\\n* Keyboard-only operation\\n* IME and composition\\n* Screen readers\\n* Clipboard sources\\n* Drag/drop\\n* Focus and overlays\\n* Large documents\\n* DOM mutation recovery\\n\\n### Frameworks\\n\\n* Vanilla reference traces\\n* React traces and SSR\\n* Svelte traces and SSR\\n* Solid traces and SSR\\n* Node-view lifecycle\\n* Subscription cleanup\\n* Hydration boundaries\\n* Framework package isolation\\n\\n### Security\\n\\n* Raw HTML policy\\n* URL sanitization\\n* Paste sanitization\\n* Embed sandboxing\\n* Asset authorization\\n* Resource exhaustion\\n* Fuzzing\\n* Collaboration authorization\\n* Snapshot validation\\n* Extension policy conflicts\\n\\n### Packaging\\n\\n* ESM consumers\\n* CommonJS consumers where promised\\n* Type declarations\\n* Tree shaking\\n* Side-effect declarations\\n* Browser/server entry separation\\n* Export maps\\n* Packed installs\\n* Workspace-boundary verifier\\n* Minimum supported runtimes\\n\\n## Performance budgets to define in Phase 0\\n\\nSet explicit budgets for:\\n\\n* Initial parse by document size\\n* Incremental edit and keystroke latency\\n* Markdown serialization latency\\n* Source/visual mode switch latency\\n* Memory by document size\\n* DOM nodes and viewport rendering\\n* Clipboard import latency\\n* Collaboration update size and fan-out\\n* Snapshot load and compaction\\n* Server render throughput\\n\\nBudgets should be validated on representative documents, lower-powered devices, and all supported browsers.\\n\\n## Repository placement\\n\\nCreate mdfn as a top-level multi-package function inside the root monorepo, not a nested monorepo.\\n\\nRecommended planning bundle:\\n\\n```text\\nmdfn/\\n  .conduct/\\n    MDFN-01/\\n      product.md\\n      content-model.md\\n      architecture.md\\n      extension-sdk.md\\n      security.md\\n      verification.md\\n      phases.md\\n```\\n\\nPublished function packages follow the multi-package form `@mdfn/<package>`, with the curated facade published as `mdfn`. Shared ecosystem-independent primitives belong in `packages/` only if multiple functions genuinely own the abstraction.\\n\\n## Engineering effort and team shape\\n\\nEngineering-effort bands:\\n\\n* Contracts and risk spikes: **4–6 engineer-weeks**\\n* Integrated prototype: **8–12 engineer-weeks**\\n* Production headless/browser foundation: **9–15 engineer-months**\\n* Complete self-hosted platform: **18–30 engineer-months**\\n\\nA practical team shape includes:\\n\\n* Editing/browser architecture ownership\\n* Markdown/parser and source-fidelity ownership\\n* Cross-framework and UIFn ownership\\n* Collaboration/backend ownership when Phase 5 begins\\n* Dedicated accessibility and security review capacity\\n\\nDo not convert these bands into calendar commitments until Phase 0 closes the kernel, preservation, syntax, browser, and collaboration risks.\\n\\n## Immediate next decision\\n\\nBefore implementation, approve or revise:\\n\\n 1. The three-level preservation contract\\n 2. CommonMark baseline and GFM default\\n 3. Stable versus optional package boundary\\n 4. Extension SDK responsibilities\\n 5. Framework parity contract\\n 6. Raw HTML and embed security defaults\\n 7. First stable release boundary\\n 8. DocsFn compatibility approach\\n 9. ContentFn/CmsFn migration approach\\n10. Editing-kernel and collaboration-engine spike criteria\\n\\n## Definition of ready for implementation\\n\\nThe work is ready to enter implementation only when:\\n\\n* Product scope and non-goals are approved.\\n* Preservation behavior is specified per syntax class.\\n* Public packages and dependency rules are approved.\\n* Extension conflicts and migrations are specified.\\n* Security defaults are explicit.\\n* Representative risk spikes pass.\\n* Corpus and semantic trace fixtures exist.\\n* Performance budgets are set.\\n* Ecosystem compatibility owners accept their integration contracts.\\n* Each delivery phase has executable verification and rollback criteria.\\n\\n## Backlog boundary\\n\\nThis document is a delivery plan, not an authorization to implement. [SFN-20](<https://linear.app/21n/issue/SFN-20/build-mdfn-as-the-superfunctions-markdown-authoring-platform>) remains unassigned, unscheduled, and in the SF Next backlog until it is explicitly prioritized.\",\"icon\":null,\"color\":null,\"url\":\"https://linear.app/21n/document/architecture-and-delivery-plan-sfn-20-build-mdfn-as-the-superfunctions-5398a216a19b\",\"slugId\":\"5398a216a19b\",\"createdAt\":\"2026-08-12T13:09:31.172Z\",\"updatedAt\":\"2026-08-12T13:09:32.359Z\",\"archivedAt\":null,\"creator\":{\"id\":\"3a6ed003-6380-47ef-9e7b-b2b01ebddc6a\",\"name\":\"Aravind\"},\"updatedBy\":{\"id\":\"3a6ed003-6380-47ef-9e7b-b2b01ebddc6a\",\"name\":\"Aravind\"},\"project\":null,\"initiative\":null,\"team\":null,\"issue\":{\"id\":\"SFN-20\",\"title\":\"Build mdfn as the Superfunctions Markdown authoring platform\"}}"
