Review result: **NO-GO** for SFN-20. I found 11 P1 and 3 P2 issues. This is a promising prototype, but it does not satisfy the [Linear production-ready contract](https://linear.app/21n/issue/SFN-20/build-mdfn-as-the-superfunctions-markdown-authoring-platform).

::code-comment{title="[P1] Preserve disabled syntax as opaque" body="The baseline parser only treats unknown mdast node types as opaque. Unsupported directives and frontmatter are instead interpreted as ordinary CommonMark nodes with no diagnostic. Reproduced: editing :::unknown changed its closing fence, while editing frontmatter normalized --- to ***, violating touched-region preservation." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/markdown/src/index.ts" start=220 end=230 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Preserve extension nodes in visual mode" body="The fallback converts every unrecognized extension node into a paragraph. A directive-callout document round-trips through the visual projection as paragraph, losing its type and behavior. The DOM extension-renderer contract needs to be implemented instead of silently degrading nodes." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/dom/src/schema.ts" start=91 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Enforce URL policy in the visual editor" body="Link marks emit href directly without the renderer URL policy. Reproduced Markdown containing a javascript URL reaching the ProseMirror document unchanged, so unsafe links can be placed in the interactive editor DOM through parsing or paste." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/dom/src/schema.ts" start=46 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Sanitize extension renderer output" body="Extension HTML is returned directly before any raw-HTML, URL, or sanitization policy. A registered extension can currently render script elements and event handlers verbatim. Extension output must be inert or pass through a mandatory host sanitizer." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/render/src/index.ts" start=135 end=138 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Validate the cached document identity" body="A matching schema hash causes the supplied cached document to be trusted, but sourceHash authenticates only the Markdown string. Reproduced a snapshot whose Markdown was valid but whose document contained arbitrary forged content; restoreSnapshot returned the forged tree. Reparse or bind the cache to a verified document/source identity." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/core/src/state.ts" start=50 end=52 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Use one history and selection authority" body="ProseMirror owns one history stack while the controller records every ProseMirror edit in another, and selection-only ProseMirror transactions never reach the controller. Reproduced a visual undo restoring the original source followed by controller undo reapplying the edit. History, selection, and commands must be driven through one shared semantic engine." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/dom/src/index.ts" start=81 end=99 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Revalidate collaboration metadata" body="Schema compatibility is checked only when the session is created. A remote Yjs update can subsequently replace metadata.schemaHash and is accepted without negotiation or rejection; this was reproduced with an incompatible hash. Remote sidecar JSON is also parsed after the Yjs document has already mutated, allowing malformed state to leave the controller stale." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/collab/src/index.ts" start=83 end=95 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Require atomic persistence writes" body="Adapters without transaction support execute document updates, immutable revision insertion, and idempotency receipt insertion as independent writes. Failure after the document update leaves missing history or receipts and makes retries unsafe. Either require transactions for these operations or provide an atomic adapter-level operation." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/server/src/index.ts" start=95 end=97 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Actually adopt mdfn in DocsFn" body="The mdfn parse result is discarded and DocsFn immediately compiles the same source through its existing parseBlocks and marked pipeline. This does not replace duplicated Markdown interpretation or create the promised compatibility projection; it merely adds validation work." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/docsfn/core/src/markdown.ts" start=731 end=740 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Honor the ContentFn Markdown policy" body="The widget always creates the default GFM editor and receives neither dialect nor allowRawHtml from the ContentFn field definition. A commonmark field is therefore authored with GFM semantics, and future policy changes can reinterpret persisted strings. Pass and persist the full Markdown content contract." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/cmsfn/studio/src/editor/widgets/MarkdownWidget.tsx" start=14 end=15 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P1] Exercise real adapters in parity tests" body="This test records one controller trace, copies it, and changes only the framework label. React, Svelte, Solid, and vanilla DOM are never mounted or driven through the same semantic inputs, so the advertised parity gate cannot detect their divergent history, selection, lifecycle, or rendering behavior." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/adapter-kit/src/adapter.test.ts" start=26 end=30 priority=1}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Do not consume following blank lines" body="The closing-fence expression uses whitespace-star, which also consumes newlines. Reproduced editing a directive with a blank line after its fence deleting that blank line. Restrict trailing whitespace to horizontal characters and handle the line ending separately." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/extensions/src/index.ts" start=55 end=58 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Build or remove wildcard subpaths" body="The export map promises arbitrary extension subpaths, but the build emits only dist/index files. Reproduced importing @mdfn/extensions/callout failing with ERR_MODULE_NOT_FOUND. Add real subpath entry points or expose only the root export." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/mdfn/extensions/package.json" start=9 end=11 priority=2}

::code-comment{title="[P2] Align downstream Node support" body="ContentFn server still advertises Node 18.18 while the new @mdfn/markdown dependency declares Node 20 through 24. Engine-strict consumers on the currently supported ContentFn range cannot install this graph; update the downstream engine range or support Node 18 in mdfn." file="/Users/serro/Documents/dev/n/worktrees/superfunctions/mdfn-SFN-20/contentfn/server/package.json" start=42 end=53 priority=2}

